{"title":"CLI","slug":"CLI","html":"<p>CLI can refer to multiple things:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a class=\"ext wk-missing\" href=\"https://wiki.osdev.org/Common_Language_Infrastructure\" rel=\"noopener\">Common Language Infrastructure</a> of the .NET framework</li>\n<li><a data-wiki=\"Command Line\" href=\"#/library/Command_Line\">Command Line</a> Interface</li>\n<li><a data-wiki=\"Interrupts\" href=\"#/library/Interrupts\">CLear Interrupt</a> flag - An assembly instruction to disable all interrupts</li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[],"categories":["OS theory"],"rating":null,"flags":[],"words":27,"summary":"","updated":"2023-07-10","authors":["Khaledhammouda"],"url":"https://wiki.osdev.org/CLI","history":"https://wiki.osdev.org/index.php?title=CLI&action=history","backlinks":[{"t":"Babystep2","s":"Babystep2"},{"t":"CIL","s":"CIL"}],"lessons":[]}